## Value Objects (src/domain/value_objects/)
Add 10 new validated value objects covering core domain primitives:
- Cpf       — 11-digit Brazilian CPF with modulo-11 check-digit algorithm;
              rejects all-identical-digit sequences
- Cnpj      — 14-digit Brazilian CNPJ with dual check-digit validation
- Currency  — integer-cents monetary value; fromDecimal() factory rounds
              floating-point input; add/subtract/isNegative helpers
- Username  — 3-50 chars, letters/digits/_/- only, no spaces
- Name      — firstName + lastName pair, 2-100 chars each, Unicode letters,
              spaces, hyphens, apostrophes (replaces single-string variant)
- Protocol  — uppercase alphanumeric identifier (e.g. HTTP, PROT-2024-0001);
              rejects leading/trailing hyphens
- AccessToken — JWT-format bearer token (header.payload.signature); max 2 048
                chars; getPayloadSegment() helper
- File      — in-memory file buffer with MIME type, size validation (≤ 50 MB),
              and buffer-length / declared-size consistency check
- BirthDate — validates past date, age 0–150 years; getAge() computed against
              today; toISOString() returns YYYY-MM-DD
- Document  — generic official document with DocumentType discriminator
              (CPF | CNPJ | PASSPORT | RG); alphanumeric + -./
## i18n for Enum Validation Errors
Apply t() to all five domain enum create() factory methods so error
messages are localised and maintainable:
- TransactionTypeEnum  → enum.transaction_type.invalid
- PaginationOrder      → enum.pagination_order.invalid
- UserStatusEnum       → enum.user_status.invalid
- RoleEnum             → enum.role.invalid
- AttachmentFileTypeEnum → enum.attachment_file_type.invalid
Five corresponding keys added to src/application/i18n/locales/en.ts.
All messages use {value} interpolation so the invalid input is visible
in the thrown InvalidDataFormatException message.
## Request Duration Logging (LoggerInterceptor)
Instrument every HTTP/RPC request with wall-clock timing via rxjs tap():
  import { tap } from 'rxjs/operators';
  const startedAt = Date.now();
  return next.handle().pipe(
    tap(() => request.logger.debug({ durationMs: Date.now() - startedAt })),
  );
Timing is logged at debug level on the per-request child logger (which
already carries loggerId), consistent with the project Logger convention.
## Bug Fix — attachment/get_all.usecase.ts
IPaginationResponse does not expose totalItems; changed the result-count
log call from result.totalItems to result.items.length, matching the
pattern used in all other get_all use cases.
